        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Tiddly-Wink British',
            subtitle: 'Domino Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tiddly-Wink British is a domino connecting game in the Block family. Players receive tiles from a double-six set (or double-nine or double-twelve for more players), the holder of the largest double leads, and tiles are played on either end of the line with matching ends. Playing a double gives the option of a second tile in the same turn. The winner is the player who dominoes, or the player with the lowest pip count if the game is blocked.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: USA\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
